    f"R316 RayLayers was reused on local proposals: {doc['cache']['evaluations']} cached evaluations, median {doc['cache']['median_reused_beads']:.0f}/{doc['cache']['median_total_layers']:.0f} body layers reused. Global shape/registration changes used R315 refined tracing. These are run diagnostics, not a new matched speedup claim. Every selected target-grid owner raster is compared directly against the R315 reference.\n",
    'The joint candidate uses compact cant coefficients −1/−3/−3/0/0° at centers −13/0/+13/−26/+26. Shared axial thickness rises about 2.8% relative to R316, while global tilt falls about 1.1° and elevation 1.3°. These are conditional fit preferences, not measured dimensions or camera calibration. Saved phase/station/tilt arrays include two unused trailing zeros inherited from repeated zero-basis extension; they are verified zero and do not add free body transforms.\n',
